# The database/ingest/ tree is developer tooling for regenerating
# processes.h5. Not part of the shipped repo — users consume
# processes.h5 directly. Kept on-disk for local rebuilds but not
# committed so PRs / checkouts stay clean.
# Exception: adas.py is the parser imported by build_processes_h5.py
# itself, so the script is broken without it on a fresh checkout.
database/ingest/*
!database/ingest/adas.py

# Local research cases that are not ready for the public repository.
# Important WIP should also be backed up: ignored files can be removed by
# `git clean -fdX`.
examples/wip/

# Private notes and reference material. Public case documentation belongs in
# README.md; use these explicit local suffixes for files that should not ship.
examples/**/NOTES.local.md
examples/**/*.local.pdf

# Sphinx build output
/docs/_build/

# WIP code in the OpenEdge package — local-only, not part of the build.
# CMake globs only src/OPENEDGE/*.cpp,h (single dir, no recurse), so
# anything inside this directory is ignored by the compiler too.
src/OPENEDGE/wip/

# Local Claude Code memory / context file (kept untracked)
CLAUDE.md

# Local planning / regeneration notes (kept on disk, not pushed)
database/iead/IEAD_REGENERATE.md

# Personal plans / TODOs / working notes — never committed (see notes/README.md)
/notes/


# Device backgrounds intentionally retained with the public workflows.
examples/workflows/particulates/st40_lithium_powder_dropper/*.html
